 Lines beginning with a semicolon are ignored.
+A line may be at most 510 characters long, not counting its newline (a
+carriage return before it counts as a character); a longer line is refused
+with an error and its tool is not loaded. While a table loaded with refused
+lines is in use, LinuxCNC refuses to save it, since that would delete those
+lines: shorten them and reload the table. A tool whose line would be too
+long to write is refused the same way. A refused save keeps the file as it
